meta {
  name: Cart
  seq: 2
}

docs {
  The full lifecycle, in order, against one visitor's cart.

  Two things make this folder work, and both are asserted rather than assumed:

  1. **The session cookie.** There is no login. `vela.session` is a signed, HttpOnly cookie
     issued on the first response of the run, and it is the only thing that decides whose
     cart these requests touch. Bruno's cookie jar carries it; "Get the empty cart" proves
     it by asserting the server did *not* issue a second one.
  2. **A real variant id.** The first two requests discover one from the catalog. Ids are
     generated when the seed is applied, so a hard-coded id would pass here and 404 in CI.

  The folder is re-runnable: it deletes the cart before it starts rather than assuming it
  begins empty. In the CLI the jar is per-run so it always would be; in the GUI the jar
  persists and it would not.
}
